{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-distance-finite","title":"prop:riemannian-distance-finite","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2269,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:riemannian-distance-finite","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-distance]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-symm]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-triangle]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:riemannian-distance-finite","line":3660,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Finiteness of the Riemannian Distance]\n\\label{prop:riemannian-distance-finite}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-distance, lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small, lem:riemannian-distance-symm, lem:riemannian-distance-triangle}\n\n\n\n\nIf $(M,g)$ is connected, then $d_g(p,q)<\\infty$ for all $p,q\\in M$. This is the finite-length conclusion associated with Proposition \\ref{prop:connected-manifold-admissible-curve}.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small,lem:riemannian-distance-symm,lem:riemannian-distance-triangle}\n\\sketch Fix $p$ and let $S=\\{q:d_g(p,q)<\\infty\\}$. It contains $p$, using the constant curve. If $q_0\\in S$, Lemmas \\ref{lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small} and \\ref{lem:riemannian-distance-triangle} give a neighborhood on which $d_g(p,\\cdot)$ remains finite, so $S$ is open. If $q_0\\notin S$, the same local bound, Lemmas \\ref{lem:riemannian-distance-triangle} and \\ref{lem:riemannian-distance-symm}, show that a nearby $q$ cannot lie in $S$, for otherwise\n\\[\nd_g(p,q_0)\\le d_g(p,q)+d_g(q,q_0)<\\infty.\n\\]\nThus $S$ is closed. Connectedness gives $S=M$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Finiteness of the Riemannian Distance] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a7269656d616e6e69616e2d64697374616e63652d66696e697465\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-distance\">↗ def:riemannian-distance</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ariemannian-distance-locally-small\">↗ lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ariemannian-distance-symm\">↗ lem:riemannian-distance-symm</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ariemannian-distance-triangle\">↗ lem:riemannian-distance-triangle</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> is connected, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d_g(p,q)&lt;\\infty $\">$d_g(p,q)&lt;\\infty $</span> for all <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p,q\\in M$\">$p,q\\in M$</span>. This is the finite-length conclusion associated with Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aconnected-manifold-admissible-curve\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:connected-manifold-admissible-curve\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a636f6e6e65637465642d6d616e69666f6c642d61646d69737369626c652d6375727665\">15</a>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ariemannian-distance-locally-small\">↗ lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ariemannian-distance-symm\">↗ lem:riemannian-distance-symm</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ariemannian-distance-triangle\">↗ lem:riemannian-distance-triangle</a> \\sketch Fix <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S=\\{ q:d_g(p,q)&lt;\\infty \\} $\">$S=\\{ q:d_g(p,q)&lt;\\infty \\} $</span>. It contains <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>, using the constant curve. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q_0\\in S$\">$q_0\\in S$</span>, Lemmas <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ariemannian-distance-locally-small\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7269656d616e6e69616e2d64697374616e63652d6c6f63616c6c792d736d616c6c\">15</a> and <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ariemannian-distance-triangle\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-triangle\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7269656d616e6e69616e2d64697374616e63652d747269616e676c65\">15</a> give a neighborhood on which <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d_g(p,\\cdot )$\">$d_g(p,\\cdot )$</span> remains finite, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S$\">$S$</span> is open. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q_0\\notin S$\">$q_0\\notin S$</span>, the same local bound, Lemmas <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ariemannian-distance-triangle\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-triangle\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7269656d616e6e69616e2d64697374616e63652d747269616e676c65\">15</a> and <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ariemannian-distance-symm\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-symm\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7269656d616e6e69616e2d64697374616e63652d73796d6d\">15</a>, show that a nearby <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span> cannot lie in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S$\">$S$</span>, for otherwise </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  d_g(p,q_0)\\le d_g(p,q)+d_g(q,q_0)&lt;\\infty .  \\]\">\\[  d_g(p,q_0)\\le d_g(p,q)+d_g(q,q_0)&lt;\\infty .  \\]</span></p><p> Thus <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S$\">$S$</span> is closed. Connectedness gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S=M$\">$S=M$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-small-implies-nearby","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:metric-preserving-distance-le","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-distance","title":"def:riemannian-distance","label":"def:riemannian-distance"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small","title":"lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small","label":"lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-symm","title":"lem:riemannian-distance-symm","label":"lem:riemannian-distance-symm"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-triangle","title":"lem:riemannian-distance-triangle","label":"lem:riemannian-distance-triangle"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:connected-manifold-admissible-curve","title":"prop:connected-manifold-admissible-curve","label":"prop:connected-manifold-admissible-curve"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:connected-manifold-c1-curve","title":"prop:connected-manifold-c1-curve","label":"prop:connected-manifold-c1-curve"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces","title":"thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces","label":"thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-metric-space-dist","title":"lem:riemannian-metric-space-dist","label":"lem:riemannian-metric-space-dist"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-distance-finite","title":"prop:riemannian-distance-finite","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[Finiteness of the Riemannian Distance]\n\\label{prop:riemannian-distance-finite}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-distance, lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small, lem:riemannian-distance-symm, lem:riemannian-distance-triangle}\n\n\n\n\nIf $(M,g)$ is connected, then $d_g(p,q)<\\infty$ for all $p,q\\in M$. This is the finite-length conclusion associated with Proposition \\ref{prop:connected-manifold-admissible-curve}.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small,lem:riemannian-distance-symm,lem:riemannian-distance-triangle}\n\\sketch Fix $p$ and let $S=\\{q:d_g(p,q)<\\infty\\}$. It contains $p$, using the constant curve. If $q_0\\in S$, Lemmas \\ref{lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small} and \\ref{lem:riemannian-distance-triangle} give a neighborhood on which $d_g(p,\\cdot)$ remains finite, so $S$ is open. If $q_0\\notin S$, the same local bound, Lemmas \\ref{lem:riemannian-distance-triangle} and \\ref{lem:riemannian-distance-symm}, show that a nearby $q$ cannot lie in $S$, for otherwise\n\\[\nd_g(p,q_0)\\le d_g(p,q)+d_g(q,q_0)<\\infty.\n\\]\nThus $S$ is closed. Connectedness gives $S=M$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-distance","title":"def:riemannian-distance","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small","title":"lem:riemannian-distance-locally-small","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-symm","title":"lem:riemannian-distance-symm","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-distance-triangle","title":"lem:riemannian-distance-triangle","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}